<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58259" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόβᾱλ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>impudent rogue, arrant knave</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				450
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1015
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				279
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				53.3
			</span></i>; of Midias, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
			</span></i> Com.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>: in pl., <i>mischievous goblins</i>, invoked by rogues,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				635
			</span></i>; of the owl, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. καὶ μιμητής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					597b23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόβαλα, τά</span>, <i>knavish tricks, rogueries</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				417
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				104
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕβριστον ἔργον καὶ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					162
				</span></i>
			. (For the orig. sense cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοβαλεύω</span>.)</div>
